---
title: Songs
description: Make a song from a MIDI file, edit it in the Song Editor, and play it with a SONG constant.
sidebar:
  order: 4
---

A song is a `.bgm` file in `audio/songs/`, and its `SONG_` constant is named after the file, so `meadow_theme.bgm` becomes `SONG_MEADOW_THEME`. A `.bgm` file opens in the Song Editor.

## Making a song from a MIDI file

{% steps %}
1. In the Filesystem, right-click `audio/songs` and select **New > Song**.
2. Choose your MIDI file.
3. Choose the soundfont the MIDI file was made for. Most MIDI files use **General MIDI**, and each of their instruments plays the closest of the game's samples. Choose **Paper Mario** for a file made with the Paper Mario soundfont, whose instruments are the game's own samples.
4. Enter a name for the song. Diorama64 suggests one from the MIDI file's name.
5. Select **OK**.
{% /steps %}

The new song opens in the Song Editor.

To start from one of the game's songs instead, copy its file, such as `audio/songs/pleasant_path.bgm`, paste it into `audio/songs`, and rename the copy.

## Reimport the MIDI file

If you change the MIDI file that a song was made from, open the song and select **Song > Reimport MIDI**. The changes you made in the Song Editor are kept. To reimport from a different MIDI file, select **Song > Reimport MIDI From...** instead.

## Playing the song

Use the constant in the EVT script that sets a map's music:

```c
Call(SetMusic, 0, SONG_MEADOW_THEME, 0, VOL_LEVEL_FULL)
```

## Loading extra sound banks with a song

The Song Editor lists the instruments in your mod as it was the last time you played it. If you add an instrument, select **Game > Play** before you open the song.

Songs play instruments from the sound banks that are loaded when the song starts. Besides the banks that are always loaded, a song can load up to three song banks. A bank that any song loads is a song bank, and the game loads it only while such a song plays. For example, Toad Town's song loads `SPC0`.

To use an instrument from a song bank, choose it in the Song Editor's instrument list. The Song Editor saves the bank's name in the `.bgm` file, and the game loads the bank whenever it plays the song. If you start from one of the game's songs, its file already names the banks it needs.

A bank that a song loads isn't always loaded, so sound effects and ambient sounds can't play its samples. The Song Editor also lists sound effect banks, such as `SYS0` and your `SFX` banks, so don't choose instruments from those for a song. Choose instruments from the game's song banks, or from [a bank you add for your songs](/papermario-dx/audio/instruments/#adding-an-instrument-for-songs).

## Limits

The game has room for 256 songs.
